<title>SWITZERLAND: Zurich says Scudder to dilute 98 profits.</title>
<headline>Zurich says Scudder to dilute 98 profits.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Zurich Group's planned acquisition of Scudder, Stevens &amp; Clark will be slightly dilutive of earnings in 1998, chief executive Rolf Hueppi said.</p>
<p>&quot;In the first year, 1998, I think there will be a slight pressure on profit -- it will be somewhat dilutive and in the second year it will be neutral,&quot; he told reporters.  </p>
<p>Hueppi also said that the acquisition will result in goodwill writedowns of $30 million to $40 million annually over the next 20 to 25 years.</p>
<p>Before the Scudder acquisition, goodwill already on the group's non-life balance sheet totalled some 790 million Swiss francs, mainly the result of Zurich's purchase of Kemper, Hueppi said.</p>
<p>-- Zurich newsroom +41 1 631 7340</p>
